</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-11-06.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="154356"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#154356" label="[15:43:56]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; With live-bootstrap is there an easy way to drop into a shell in fiwix?</span></div><div class="line" id="155603"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#155603" label="[15:56:03]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">cosinusoidally: if you use the interactive option, you will get a shell on the 2nd virtual terminal as soon as Bash is built</span></div><div class="line" id="155658"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#155658" label="[15:56:58]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">do note that it's still the early Bash, so you need to follow each Enter press with a Ctrl+D</span></div><div class="line" id="163112"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#163112" label="[16:31:12]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; Thanks, I'll give that a go. I'm interested to see how usable the live-bootstrap build of fiwix is (eg could I bootstrap from nothing all the way up to say running Quake).</span></div><div class="line" id="170400"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#170400" label="[17:04:00]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Possibly we can try to rebuild.bash once we have autoconf</span></div><div class="line" id="170436"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#170436" label="[17:04:36]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; It might work better now</span></div><div class="line" id="170510"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#170510" label="[17:05:10]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; (One of the musl patches used to be dodgy)</span></div><div class="line" id="180555"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#180555" label="[18:05:55]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: is the first autoconf sufficient for rebuilding bash?</span></div><div class="line" id="180638"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#180638" label="[18:06:38]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(IIRC we fail on automake in WSL2 and possibly other environments, right after building the first autoconf)</span></div><div class="line" id="182641"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#182641" label="[18:26:41]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Hmm, don't remember, possibly</span></div><div class="line" id="182654"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#182654" label="[18:26:54]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; That bash quite old</span></div><div class="line" id="183707"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#183707" label="[18:37:07]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; *is quite old</span></div><br /></div></body></html>